# A missing hashed asset must return a real 404, never the SPA shell.
# Without this file Pages auto-detects the project as a single-page app and
# answers every unmatched path with index.html at status 200, text/html — for
# a module script that is the "Expected a JavaScript-or-Wasm module script but
# the server responded with a MIME type of text/html" failure. A deploy swaps
# the whole hashed-asset set, so any tab holding the previous shell trips this
# the moment it asks for a hash the new deployment no longer contains. Static
# assets always win over redirect rules; only genuinely missing /assets/*
# paths reach the 404 rule.
/assets/* /404.html 404

# SPA deep links (vue-router history mode) still need the shell — spelled out
# so the behavior no longer depends on Pages' SPA auto-detection.
/* /index.html 200
